\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Where the origin and the functional equation enter. The carrier is double-ended: the readout leg (heights \(z>1\), fiber \(W\)) and the dual leg (the \(z<1\) end, conjugate phases on the anti-helix, fiber \(W^{\vee }\)) are welded at the origin \(z=1\) --- the central point \(s=\tfrac  12\), where the weld plane meets the weld axis. The functional equation is the fold through that weld: height inversion \(z\DOTSB \mapstochar \rightarrow 1/z\) (\(s\DOTSB \mapstochar \rightarrow 1-s\)) exchanges the legs, and on the weld axis the inversion coincides with conjugation, which \(J\) supplies phasor by phasor (the carrier reflection theorem and bank reflection lemma of \cite  {UniversalCarrier}, step~1) --- no Poisson summation is consumed. The only mismatch the exchange permits is the unimodular offset at the weld, \(\varepsilon =\DOTSI \prodop \slimits@ _v(-\bar  \alpha _v)\), assembled per place in Lean (\texttt  {StrandExchange.bankProduct\_exchange} from \texttt  {ChiralityHB.symClock\_star}); \(\varepsilon \) is the root number, the offset that places or doubles the central cancellation.}}{9}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:grh-weld}{{1}{9}{Where the origin and the functional equation enter. The carrier is double-ended: the readout leg (heights \(z>1\), fiber \(W\)) and the dual leg (the \(z<1\) end, conjugate phases on the anti-helix, fiber \(W^{\vee }\)) are welded at the origin \(z=1\) --- the central point \(s=\tfrac 12\), where the weld plane meets the weld axis. The functional equation is the fold through that weld: height inversion \(z\mapsto 1/z\) (\(s\mapsto 1-s\)) exchanges the legs, and on the weld axis the inversion coincides with conjugation, which \(J\) supplies phasor by phasor (the carrier reflection theorem and bank reflection lemma of \cite {UniversalCarrier}, step~1) --- no Poisson summation is consumed. The only mismatch the exchange permits is the unimodular offset at the weld, \(\varepsilon =\prod _v(-\bar \alpha _v)\), assembled per place in Lean (\texttt {StrandExchange.bankProduct\_exchange} from \texttt {ChiralityHB.symClock\_star}); \(\varepsilon \) is the root number, the offset that places or doubles the central cancellation}{figure.1}{}}
\citation{UniversalCarrier}
